+"""Verified non-k-stability witness generator for arXiv:2307.03794.
+
+The paper's Observation 2 says that a house-allocation matching M is k-stable
+exactly when its improvement graph has no matching of size k.  This module
+inverse-generates an improvement graph as the union of cyclic perfect
+matchings, embeds it into strict preference lists above a displayed current
+matching M, and asks for a matching proving that M is not n-stable.
+
+Every cyclic layer is generated by the same rule and is a valid certificate;
+the stored answer is one layer selected before object and agent names, input
+orders, and preference orders are shuffled.  Verification checks the proposed
+alternative allocation directly and never reads the stored answer.
